  "result": "Empty search results\nNo results were found for the provided queries--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nFastidiosipila sanguinis gen. nov., sp. nov., a new Gram-positive, coccus-shaped organism from human blood | Microbiology Society (https://www.microbiologyresearch.org/content/journal/ijsem/10.1099/ijs.0.63327-0)\nciteturn98view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.microbiologyresearch.org/content/journal/ijsem/10.1099/ijs.0.63327-0\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 268\nL0: 【0†iframe†www.googletagmanager.com】\nL1: \nL2: 1887\nL3: \nL4: 【1†Skip to content】\nL5: \nL6: [Input]\nL7: \nL8: 【2†International Journal of Systematic and Evolutionary Microbiology】 【3†Volume 55, Issue 2】\nL9: # Fastidiosipila sanguinis gen. nov., sp. nov., a new Gram-positive, coccus-shaped organism from human blood 【4†Image: Free】\nL10: \nL11:   * 【5†Enevold Falsen】^{1}, 【6†Matthew D. Collins】^{2}, 【7†Christina Welinder-Olsson】^{1}, 【8†Yuli Song】^{3}, 【9†Sydney M. Finegold】^{3,4} and 【10†Paul A. Lawson】^{2}\nL12:   * 【11†View Affiliations Hide Affiliations】\nL13: ^{1} 【12†Culture Collection, Department of Clinical Bacteriology, University of Göteborg, Sweden】 ^{2} 【13†School of Food Biosciences, University of Reading, Reading, UK】 ^{3} 【14†Infectious Diseases Section, VA Medical Center, West Los Angeles, CA 90073, USA】 ^{4} 【15†Department of Medicine, UCLA School of Medicine, CA 90073, USA】\nL14: \nL15: Correspondence Paul A. Lawson\nL16:  【16†[email protected]】\nL17: \nL18:   * Published: 01 March 2005\nL19:   * 【11†info Info】\nL20:     * 【17†Article information】\nL21:     * 【18†Full-Text】\nL22:     * 【19†Figures and Tables】\nL23:     * 【20†References (27)】\nL24:     * 【21†Cited By (83)】\nL25:     * 【22†Supplementary Material】\nL26:     * 【23†Metrics】\nL27: \nL28:   * 【11†build Tools】\nL29: ### Tools\nL30: \nL31:     * 【11†Add to my favourites】\nL32: \nL33:     * 【11†Create publication alert】\nL34: \nL35: 【11†Create citation alert】\nL36: \nL37: 【11†Create correction alert】\nL38: \nL39:     * 【11†Export citation】\nL40:       * 【24†BibT_{E}X】\nL41:       * 【25†Endnote】\nL42:       * 【24†Zotero】\nL43:       * 【26†Medlars】\nL44:       * 【27†RefWorks】\nL45:       * 【28†Mendeley†www.mendeley.com】\nL46:     * 【11†Recommend to library】\nL47:     *     * [Input]\nL48: ## Abstract\nL49: Phenotypic and phylogenetic studies were performed on two strains of an unidentified Gram-positive, fastidious, non-spore-forming, coccus-shaped bacterium recovered from human blood. The organism was catalase-negative and grew under strictly anaerobic conditions and in the presence of 2 and 6 % O 2.\nL50: Comparative 16S rRNA gene sequencing demonstrated that the unidentified bacterium was, phylogenetically, far removed from peptostreptococci and related Gram-positive coccus-shaped organisms, but exhibited a phylogenetic association with Clostridium rRNA cluster III [as defined by 【29†Collins et al., Int J Syst Bacteriol 44 (1994), 812–826】 ].\nL51: Sequence divergence values of 15 % or more were observed between the unidentified bacterium and all other recognized species within this and related rRNA clostridial clusters. Treeing analysis showed that the unknown bacterium formed a deep line branching at the periphery of rRNA cluster III and represents a hitherto unknown genus within this supra-generic grouping.\nL52: On the basis of both phylogenetic and phenotypic evidence, it is proposed that the unknown bacterium from blood be classified in a new genus, Fastidiosipila gen. nov., as Fastidiosipila sanguinis sp. nov. The type strain of Fastidiosipila sanguinis is CCUG 47711 T (=CIP 108292 T).\nL53:   * Published Online: 01/03/2005\nL54: \nL55: SGM\nL56: \nL57: 【30†Image: Loading】\nL58: \nL59: Article metrics loading...\nL60: \nL61: /content/journal/ijsem/10.1099/ijs.0.63327-0\nL62: \nL63: 2005-03-01\nL64: \nL65: 2026-11-08\nL66: ## Metrics\nL67: \nL68: 【30†I